# landmark (assets/world3d/gate/landmark.set, hand-placed)
# Gate Courtyard: the gatehouse over the north door: two round towers, a hipped slate roof and lintel between, curtain walls and corner turrets either side.
# Hand-placed by the landmark pass on the room's blocked back band and what lies behind it,
# so it never stands on a tile a knight walks or hides the floor from the camera.

# the gatehouse: towers either side of the door gap, the lintel spanning it high over the road
frustum-12 stone   at 150 0 0 size 44 52 30 id lm-tower-west
cylinder-12 stone   at 150 52 0 size 48 6 32
cone-12 slate   at 150 58 0 size 42 18 40
frustum-12 stone   at 234 0 0 size 44 52 30 id lm-tower-east
cylinder-12 stone   at 234 52 0 size 48 6 32
cone-12 slate   at 234 58 0 size 42 18 40
box    stone   at 192 34 0 size 64 14 26 id lm-lintel
hip    slate   at 192 48 0 size 76 14 30 id lm-gate-roof
box    door    at 192 31 14.5 size 36 3 2
# curtain walls either side, with their merlons
box    stone   at 80 0 -2 size 76 38 22 id lm-curtain-west
box    stone   at 304 0 -2 size 88 38 22 id lm-curtain-east
box    stone   at 52 38 -2 size 9 7 22
box    stone   at 69 38 -2 size 9 7 22
box    stone   at 86 38 -2 size 9 7 22
box    stone   at 103 38 -2 size 9 7 22
box    stone   at 120 38 -2 size 9 7 22
